This Python script uses linear regression to predict salary based on years of experience. Here's a quick breakdown:

Data Loading and Preprocessing: The dataset is loaded, with X representing years of experience and y representing salary.

Train-Test Split: The data is split into training and test sets (67% for training, 33% for testing).

Model Training: A linear regression model is trained on the training data.

Prediction: The model predicts salaries for the test set.

Visualization: Scatter plots visualize the training and test data with the regression line.

Salary Predictions: The model predicts salaries for specific experience values (15, 20, 27, 4.5, 0.5 years) and prints the results.

The script provides a simple way to visualize and predict salary based on years of experience.
